204 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 89 0 R
/E (Sources are grouped into three connectivity categories, each requiring a different authentication and request-handling approach:)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
205 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 598 0 R
/E (Key-based API authentication \(Jooble, JSearch\): Requests are authenticated via a static API key, either embedded directly in the request URL \(Jooble\) or passed through dedicated headers \(X-RapidAPI-Key, X-RapidAPI-Host for JSearch\).)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
206 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 599 0 R
/E (Browser-context authentication \(FreeHire\): Rather than a formal API key, connectivity relies on replicating browser request headers \(User-Agent, Referer\) to establish a valid session with the source's internal search endpoint.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
207 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 600 0 R
/E (Proxy-mediated scraping \(Tanqeeb\): Requests are routed through the ScrapeOps Proxy API, which handles IP rotation and header simulation to bypass the source's bot-detection layer, returning the underlying page content for parsing.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
208 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 601 0 R
/E (Static file retrieval \(TapNeo\): No live connectivity is required; the dataset is downloaded once and read directly from local storage.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
