/P 90 0 R
/E (The pipeline follows a pull-based batch ingestion model: each source is queried on demand or on a scheduled basis, rather than receiving continuous data pushes. This approach was selected because:)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
223 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 614 0 R
/E (All sources expose request/response APIs \(or scrapeable pages\) rather than event streams or webhooks.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
224 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 615 0 R
/E (Job postings are inherently low-frequency data \(new listings appear over hours or days, not seconds\), making batch pulls sufficient to capture new records without unnecessary API consumption.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
225 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 616 0 R
/E (Batch ingestion aligns naturally with the Bronze-Silver-Gold layered storage model, where each run produces a traceable, timestamped raw snapshot.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
